 "answer": "To generate embeddings using the Ollama API, you should call the `/api/embed` endpoint. The endpoint takes a JSON payload as input, which includes the model you want to use and the text input for which you want to generate embeddings.\n\nHere's how you can call the endpoint using cURL:\n\n```shell\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:11434/api/embed \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model\": \"embeddinggemma\",\n    \"input\": \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\"\n  }'\n```\n\nThe JSON payload includes:\n\n- `\"model\"`: The name of the embedding model you want to use, such as `\"embeddinggemma\"`.\n- `\"input\"`: The text string for which you want to generate embeddings, such as `\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\"`.\n\nThis information is found in the document [1] at lines 8-63, specifically under the \"Generate embeddings\" section. [ollama/docs/capabilities/embeddings.md](#).\n\nAdditionally, for generating a batch of embeddings, you can pass an array of strings to the `\"input\"` field, as shown in the same document at lines 65-114. [ollama/docs/capabilities/embeddings.md](#).",
